# AUB Functionality Matrix

Whenever any task changes user-visible functionality, UI, API capability, routes, permissions, roles, access control, account behavior, student / parent / teacher / administration functionality, file or document access, schedule, attendance, messages, payments, assessments, productions, or any other product capability, you MUST review and update `docs/Product/FUNCTIONALITY_MATRIX.md` before considering the task complete.

This file is the living product passport. It describes what each of Administration, Student, Parent, and Teacher can do **today**. Code is the source of truth. Do not copy Cursor Work Reports into the matrix.

## How to update

1. Do not change `Last updated` if the functional state did not change.
2. If a feature is added: add or update the matching row (status, channel, notes, restrictions).
3. If a feature is removed: delete the row or change the status.
4. If a permission changed: update that actor/role, including the restrictions lists.
5. Backend without UI: `🔵 Foundation / backend ready`, never `✅`.
6. UI exists but the flow is incomplete: `🟡 Partial`.
7. Idea only: `⚪ Planned`, and keep it in **Planned / next major capabilities** if it is a major module.
8. Usable through the intended UI/API: `✅ Implemented`.
9. Out of scope or blocked by design: `🚫 Not available / intentionally restricted`.
10. Do not mix actor type (Student / Parent / Teacher) with staff web roles. A Teacher app account is not Administration.

Do not invent product capabilities from old README or roadmap text.

## After every task

In the Cursor Work Report (not in the user-facing reply when the project requires only `готово`), record:

```text
FUNCTIONALITY_MATRIX updated: yes/no
```

If `no`, explain why the change did not affect product functionality.
